/-!
# Critical-pair orbit matching

This export collects the literal natural/dual pure-orbit and singular-diagonal
matching lemmas used in the terminal rank-one and rank-two argument.  The
commutator-image consumers construct the common pure vector in both symmetric
profiles and exclude movement on a denominator/support intersection in the
asymmetric case. The selected-endpoint bridge constructs the original
critical pair, both denominator ranks and the opposite central point inside
the commutator. The rank-profile extension proves the singular images from
the marked quadratic actions in both symmetric ranks, and derives the
asymmetric contradiction from the actual denominator index and dual actions.
The single-component application derives the non-FF and two-rank facts and
selects the endpoint from a faithfully embedded natural--dual pair. It proves
support preservation from the quadratic budget, retaining the reversal
transporter to handle the literal inverse-conjugate actor. The marked component
sections, their kernels and fixed-factor decomposition remain earlier-source
inputs; the component exclusions and source construction are still required.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, 14.6.20--24(4), printed pp.1038--1041.
-/
